{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"attributes"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SD","text":"Dictionary"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_NodeAttr","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Yorkie0A12_V1_NodeAttrV","text":"Yorkie_V1_NodeAttr"},{"kind":"text","text":"> { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"set"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan"]]},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Yorkie"}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"attributes","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Dictionary","preciseIdentifier":"s:SD","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Yorkie_V1_NodeAttr","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Yorkie0A12_V1_NodeAttrV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","title":"attributes","externalID":"s:6Yorkie0A19_V1_TreeRestoreSpanV10attributesSDySSAA0a1_B9_NodeAttrVGvp"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan\/attributes"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_treerestorespan\/attributes"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Yorkie_V1_NodeAttr":{"title":"Yorkie_V1_NodeAttr","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Yorkie_V1_NodeAttr"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_NodeAttr","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Yorkie_V1_NodeAttr"}],"url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_nodeattr","abstract":[]},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie":{"role":"collection","title":"Yorkie","type":"topic","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/yorkie"},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"TreeRestoreSpan carries a tree node run from a single deletion, addressed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by TreeNodeID identity, for identity-preserving Tree undo\/redo. Unlike the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text RestoreSpan (flat offsets), a tree span records the node’s structure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(type\/attrs) and its position anchors, because in a tree id-order is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sibling-order: left_sibling_id and right_sibling_id are redundant external"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary anchors of the deleted run, so restore can reconstruct the run’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internal order from the op’s own spans and needs only one surviving"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary to place it. value\/attributes are a deep copy so a GC-purged node"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be recreated."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","kind":"identifier"}],"iden